votes:
- motion: The school board recommends to the city council that it submit two questions
    to a November, 2025 referendum seeking authorization to finance improvements to
    the South Portland High School athletic complex. The subject of one question shall
    be the issuance of general obligation bonds in a principal amount not to exceed
    $4,660,000 for improvements to the South Portland High School athletic complex,
    including one new track, one natural grass stadium field, new lighting and permanent
    bathrooms. The subject of another question shall be the issuance of general obligation
    bonds in a principal amount not to exceed $5,490,000 for improvements to the South
    Portland High School athletic complex, including one new track, one synthetic
    turf stadium field, new lighting and permanent bathrooms.
  result: Passed
  count: 5 in favor, 1 opposed
  moved_2nd: Rosemarie DeAngelis, Ratliff
- motion: To recommend to the city council that the natural grass option for the South
    Portland High School athletic complex improvements be listed as the first question
    on the November 2025 referendum ballot.
  result: Passed
